1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,018
The better question came from a nurse in the maternity house: whose family is this, biologically speaking?

2
00:00:07,018 --> 00:00:15,802
A baby had two mothers on the form — one who carried him and one who would raise him — and the old system had only one line for both.

3
00:00:15,802 --> 00:00:21,946
A great part of the control belonged to whoever wrote the first column.

4
00:00:21,946 --> 00:00:29,620
The head of the department, a modern man with a quiet voice, asked what a fingerprint was for.

5
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:33,534
“Identification,” the deputy said.

6
00:00:33,534 --> 00:00:36,274
“No,” the nurse said.

7
00:00:36,274 --> 00:00:46,413
“It is a pure fact that has nothing to do with kin.” There was a little contempt in the room, and a great deal of envy.

8
00:00:46,413 --> 00:00:52,112
A priest, a spouse, a parent, and a student stood around the table.

9
00:00:52,112 --> 00:00:57,931
“The whole function of a form is to decide what counts,” the priest said.

10
00:00:57,931 --> 00:01:15,439
“A palm, a wound, a bite on the arm: three ways of saying the same thing.” Half the name, a figure, an active feature of the throat: the primitive grammar of the form decided everything before the nurse spoke.

11
00:01:15,439 --> 00:01:19,823
The president of the union wrote it down.

12
00:01:19,823 --> 00:01:29,807
A sympathetic social worker showed them a secret file with a facial photograph of a baby, a blood test, and a feeding schedule.

13
00:01:29,807 --> 00:01:34,096
“Is that biology or care?” she asked.

14
00:01:34,096 --> 00:01:36,956
“Both,” Maya said.

15
00:01:36,956 --> 00:01:46,075
“And the form makes you choose.” A black cat crossed the litter in the yard, indifferent to all of it.

16
00:01:46,075 --> 00:01:53,319
The envelope on the table contained two forms: one biological, one social.

17
00:01:53,319 --> 00:02:02,348
“Which one does the breast belong to,” the nurse asked, “when the baby will not feed?” Nobody answered.

18
00:02:02,348 --> 00:02:15,186
The baby was weighed again, the figures were written down, and the second mother came back from the corridor with a bottle and a blanket, then carried the empty tray away.

19
00:02:15,186 --> 00:02:21,205
The expansive claim — that a commune could replace a family — was met with silence.

20
00:02:21,205 --> 00:02:31,898
“A relay is not a race,” Lin wrote, “and a harness is not a horse.” The oceanic feeling of the room was mostly fatigue.

21
00:02:31,898 --> 00:02:36,893
“Something has to change in the double column,” the nurse said.

22
00:02:36,893 --> 00:02:53,941
“The skin of the form, not the skin of the child.” Of course the father of the second mother was sure that the form would lose the case; but a person who has never filled in such a form has no idea what it costs.
